nto hundreds of thousands, ten thousands, thousands, etc.:\n\n180,375 = 100,000 + 80,000 + 300 + 70 + 5\n\n698,507 = 600,000 + 90,000 + 8,000 + 500 + 0 + 7\n\nNow adding each part:\n\n100,000 + 600,000 = 700,000\n\n80,000 + 90,000 = 170,000\n\n8,000 (from second number only, since first had 0 thousands)\n\n300 + 500 = 800\n\n70 + 0 = 70\n\n5 +7 = 12\n\nAdding all together:\n\n700,000 + 170,000 = 870,000\n\n870,000 + 8,000 = 878,000\n\n878,000 + 800 = 878,800\n\n878,800 + 70 = 878,870\n\n878,870 + 12 = 878,882\n\nOkay, that seems to confirm the previous result. Hmm. So maybe my first calculation was correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method: rounding.\n\nLet me see, 180,375 is close to 180,000 and 698,507 is close to 700,000. Adding those gives 880,000. But since I rounded 180,375 up by 375 and 698,507 down by 1,493, so the total adjustment would be 375 - 1,493 = -1,118. Therefore, subtracting 1,118 from 880,000 gives 878,882. That also matches. \n\nHmm, so three different methods give the same result. Maybe I was just overthinking earlier. The answer should be 878,882. \n\nWait, but just to be absolutely sure, let me do the addition once again step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5 + 7 = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 7 + 0 = 7 +1 =8. \n\nHundreds: 3 +5 =8.\n\nThousands: 0 +8=8.\n\nTen thousands: 8 +9=17 \u2192 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 +6 +1=8.\n\nSo writing all digits: 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 2 (ones). So 878,882. \n\nYes, that's consistent. I think that's correct. Therefore, the sum is 878,882.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 180375 and 698507 is \\boxed{878882}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 180,375 and 698,507, we can add the numbers step by step by aligning them vertically and adding each column from right to left:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  \\ 180375 \\\\\n+ 698507 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n- Ones place: \\(5 + 7 = 12\\). Write down 2, carry over 1.\n- Tens place: \\(7 + 0 + 1 = 8\\). Write down 8.\n- Hundreds place: \\(3 + 5 = 8\\). Write down 8.\n- Thousands place: \\(0 + 8 = 8\\). Write down 8.\n- Ten thousands place: \\(8 + 9 = 17\\). Write down 7, carry over 1.\n- Hundred thousands place: \\(1 + 6 + 1 = 8\\). Write down 8.\n\nPutting all the digits together, we get the result 878,882.\n\nVerification using different methods (breaking down numbers, rounding, and re-adding) confirms the result. \n\nThe sum of 180,375 and 698,507 is \\(\\boxed{878882}\\).",
