ousands place) +1 (from second number's thousands place) =8, plus the 1 carried over is 9. So write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands: 9 (from first number) +2 (from second number) =11. So write 1 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 (from first number) +5 (from second number) =6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So 7.\n\nPutting all digits together: 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
