8}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem of adding 624,677 and 491,881, we can align the numbers by their place values and add column by column from right to left:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  \\ 624677 \\\\\n+ 491881 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n1. **Ones place**: \\(7 + 1 = 8\\)\n2. **Tens place**: \\(7 + 8 = 15\\) (write down 5, carry over 1)\n3. **Hundreds place**: \\(6 + 8 + 1 = 15\\) (write down 5, carry over 1)\n4. **Thousands place**: \\(4 + 1 + 1 = 6\\) (no carryover)\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \\(2 + 9 = 11\\) (write down 1, carry over 1)\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \\(6 + 4 + 1 = 11\\) (write down 11)\n\nCombining all the results from each column, we get the sum as follows:\n\n- Millions place: 1\n- Hundred thousands place: 1\n- Ten thousands place: 1\n- Thousands place: 6\n- Hundreds place: 5\n- Tens place: 5\n- Ones place: 8\n\nThus, the sum of 624,677 and 491,881 is \\(\\boxed{1116558}\\).",
