d 1 makes 8. Write down 8.\n5. **Ten-thousands place**: \\(6 + 6 = 12\\). Write down 2, carry over 1.\n6. **Hundred-thousands place**: \\(2 + 7 = 9\\), plus the carried 1 makes 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nThe carried over 1 from the hundred-thousands place is added as a new digit at the beginning, resulting in the total:\n\n\\[\n1,028,182\n\\]\n\nVerification by breaking down the numbers into parts confirms the result:\n\n\\[\n263,666 + 764,516 = 1,028,182\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\nThe sum of 263,666 and 764,516 is \\boxed{1028182}.",
