can't have 11, so that would carry over. Since 11 in the hundred thousands place is actually 1,100,000. So we need to carry over 1 to the millions place. .\n\nWait, so the total would be 1 (million) and 1 (hundred thousand). Let me write it step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 6 = 6.\n\nTens: 3 + 4 = 7.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 7 = 8.\n\nThousands: 1 + 7 = 8.\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 0 = 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 4 = 11. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
