9.\n- Tens: 1.\n- Units: 2.\n\nSecond number: 753,816.\nBreaking it down:.\n- Hundred thousands: 7.\n- Ten thousands: 5.\n- Thousands: 3.\n- Hundreds: 8.\n- Tens: 1.\n- Units: 6.\n\nAdding each column:.\n\nUnits: 2 + 6 = 8.\nTens: 1 + 1 = 2.\nHundreds: 9 + 8 = 17 (carry over 1).\nThousands: 0 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 4.\nTen thousands: 6 + 5 = 11 (carry over 1).\nHundred thousands: 9 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 17.\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 8.\nTens: 2.\nHundreds: 7 (with a carry).\nThousands: 4.\nTen thousands: 1 (and carry over 1).\nHundred thousands: 17.\n\nWait, so the ten thousands place is 11, so we write 1 there and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands. Then the hundred thousands place becomes 9+7+1=17. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
