 3 = 12, plus the 1 is 13. So 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 6 (from first) + 3 (from second) = 9, plus 1 = 10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 (from first) + 2 (from second) = 4, plus 1 = 5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place: 5 (from first) + 9 (from second) = 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 (from first) + 9 (from second) = 12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13. So write 3 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, we add that 1 as a new digit at the beginning. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
