en subtract 26 gives 1,340,803. Yep, that also works. So that confirms it again.\n\nHmm, so seems like the answer is 1,340,803. Wait, but let me just do a quick check with approximate numbers. 665,829 is roughly 666,000 and 674,974 is roughly 675,000. Adding those gives 666k +675k=1,341,000. Our answer is 1,340,803 which is 197 less than 1,341,000. That makes sense because we rounded 665,829 up by 171 (since 665,829 to 666,000 is +171) and 674,974 rounded up by 26 (since 674,974 to 675,000 is +26). So total overestimation was 171 +26=197. Hence the exact answer is 1,341,000 -197=1,340,803. That checks out. Okay, so I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in my calculations. So the sum should be 1,340,803.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 665829 and 674974 is \\boxed{1340803}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 665,829 and 674,974, we start by aligning the numbers vertically and adding each column from right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  665829 \\\\\n+ 674974 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n1. **Ones place:** \\(9 + 4 = 13\\)  \n   - Write down 3, carry over 1.\n\n2. **Tens place:** \\(2 + 7 + 1 = 10\\)  \n   - Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:** \\(8 + 9 + 1 = 18\\)  \n   - Write down 8, carry over 1.\n\n4. **Thousands place:** \\(5 + 4 + 1 = 10\\)  \n   - Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:** \\(6 + 7 + 1 = 14\\)  \n   - Write down 4, carry over 1.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:** \\(6 + 6 + 1 = 13\\)  \n   - Write down 3, carry over 1.\n\n7. **Millions place:** The carried over 1.\n\nPutting it all together, the result is 1,340,803.\n\nVerification by breaking into parts:\n- \\(665,829 = 600,000 + 60,000 + 5,000 + 800 + 20 + 9\\)\n- \\(674,974 = 600,000 + 70,000 + 4,000 + 900 + 70 + 4\\)\n\nAdding each part:\n- \\(600,000 + 600,000 = 1,200,000\\)\n- \\(60,000 + 70,000 = 130,000\\)\n- \\(5,000 + 4,000 = 9,000\\)\n- \\(800 + 900 = 1,700\\)\n- \\(20 + 70 = 90\\)\n- \\(9 + 4 = 13\\)\n\nSu