 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) = 8. Correct.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 (from first) + 0 (from second) = 3. That's good.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 + 2 = 8. So putting all those together: 8 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 9 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
