t, after adding the hundred thousands place, which is the sixth digit from the right, the result was 15. So the digit in the hundred thousands place becomes 5, and we carry over 1 to the millions place. Therefore, the total is 1,551,482. Yes, that's exactly the same as before.\n\nHmm, so both methods give me the same answer, so I feel confident that's correct. But let me try adding them in a different way, perhaps by rounding or adjusting numbers to make the addition easier.\n\nFor instance, maybe adjust 750,152 to 750,000 and 801,330 to 801,000, then add the differences.\n\n750,000 + 801,000 = 1,551,000.\n\nNow, the original numbers are 750,152 and 801,330. So the difference between 750,152 and 750,000 is +152, and between 801,330 and 801,000 is +330. Therefore, total difference is 152 + 330 = 482. Adding that to the 1,551,000 gives 1,551,482. Same result again.\n\nAlright, that's three different methods all leading to the same answer. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Let me just do a quick check using another approach, perhaps subtracting to see if the answer makes sense.\n\nSuppose the sum is 1,551,482. If I subtract one of the numbers, say 750,152, from the total, I should get the other number, 801,330.\n\nSo 1,551,482 - 750,152.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n1,551,482 minus 700,000 is 851,482.\n\nThen subtract 50,152 more (since 750,152 is 700k + 50,152):\n\n851,482 - 50,000 = 801,482.\n\nThen subtract 152: 801,482 - 152 = 801,330. Perfect, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, subtract 801,330 from the total to see if we get 750,152.\n\n1,551,482 - 800,000 = 751,482.\n\nThen subtract 1,330 more: 751,482 - 1,000 = 750,482; then minus 330: 750,482 - 330 = 750,152. Exactly. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, I can confirm that the sum is indeed 1,551,482. I think that's correct.\n\nJust to recap, in case I miscounted any zeros or misplaced a digit. Let's re-express both numbers with commas for clarity:\n\n750,152 is seven hundred fifty tho