 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands) with a carryover, and then 1 (hundred thousands) plus the carryover gives 12? Wait, maybe I need to write it out step by step again to check for errors.\n\nWait, let me do the addition step by step again carefully.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned properly:.\n\n\u2003517,120.\n+691,472.\n----------.\n\nBreaking down each digit:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n0 + 2 = 2.\n\nTens place:.\n2 + 7 = 9.\n\nHundreds place:.\n1 + 4 = 5.\n\nThousands place:.\n7 (from 517,120) + 1 (from 691,472) = 8.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n1 (from 517,120) + 9 (from 691,472) = 10. So write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n5 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So here, we write down 2 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nSince there are no digits beyond the hundred thousands place, that carried over 1 becomes the millions place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
