undred-thousands place.\n\nThen the hundred-thousands place: 4 + 3 = 7, plus the carried-over 1 makes 8. .\n\nPutting all the digits together: 8 (hundred-thousands), 0 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 4 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
