wn 1, carry over 1.\n5. **Ten-thousands place**: \\(9 + 3 = 12\\), plus the carried over 1 gives \\(13\\). Write down 3, carry over 1.\n6. **Hundred-thousands place**: \\(9 + 1 = 10\\), plus the carried over 1 gives \\(11\\). Write down 11.\n\nCombining all the digits with their respective places, we get the result 1,131,599. Verifications using different methods (breaking down numbers, approximation, and step-by-step addition) confirm the result.\n\nThe sum of 991,841 and 139,758 is \\(\\boxed{1131599}\\).",
