ust to make sure, maybe adding in another way. Let me convert both numbers to expanded form.\n\n132,304 = 100,000 + 30,000 + 2,000 + 300 + 0 +4\n\n758,009 = 700,000 +50,000 +8,000 +0 +0 +9.\n\nAdding the components:\n\n100,000 +700,000 =800,000\n\n30,000 +50,000 =80,000\n\n2,000 +8,000 =10,000\n\n300 +0 =300\n\n0 +0 =0\n\n4+9=13.\n\nNow summing all these:\n\n800,000 +80,000 =880,000\n\n880,000 +10,000=890,000\n\n890,000 +300=890,300\n\n890,300 +0=890,300\n\n890,300 +13=890,313.\n\nYes, same result. So I think 890,313 is correct. I don't see any errors in the steps. Maybe I can check with subtraction. Let me see if 890,313 - 132,304 equals 758,009.\n\nCalculating 890,313 - 132,304:\n\n890,313 minus 100,000 is 790,313.\n\n790,313 minus 32,304 (since 132,304 -100,000=32,304). \n\nWait, perhaps another way:\n\n890,313 - 132,304:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n3-4. Can't do that, borrow.\n\n13-4=9, but the tens digit is 1 (from 890,313's tens place is 1). Wait, let me write it out:\n\n\u2003890,313\n\n-132,304\n\n------------\n\nStarting from ones:\n\n3-4. Can't do that, so borrow 1 from the tens place. The tens digit is 1, so it becomes 0, and the ones become 13. 13-4=9.\n\nTens place: 0 -0 (but we had borrowed 1, so it's 0-1= -1? Wait, no. Wait, the tens digit in the top number is 1, but we borrowed 1 for the ones place, so it's now 0. The tens digit in the lower number is 0. So 0 - 0? Wait but actually, the lower number's tens digit is 0. Wait, let me structure this properly.\n\nWait, let me write it down step by step:\n\nHundreds digit: 3 (from 890,313) minus 3 (from 132,304) =0.\n\nWait maybe I need to write each digit:\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned:\n\n        8 9 0 , 3 1 3\n\n      - 1 3 2 , 3 0 4\n\n-----------------------\n\nStarting from the ones place:\n\nOnes: 3 -4. Can't do that, so borrow 1 from the tens.\n\nTens place is 1, so it becomes 0, and the ones become 13. 13-4=9.\n\nTens place: Now 0 (after borrowing) minus 0 (from the lower number's tens place