ed 10, plus the carryover 1 makes 11. So that gives 1 in that place and carryover 1. Wait, but when I did it before, I had written 1 in the ten thousands place? Wait, let me see:.\n\nWait, the columns from right to left are:.\n\nOnes: 3+5=8.\n\nTens: 2+9=11, so 1 and carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 2+7=9 +1=10, so 0 and carryover 1.\n\nThousands:7+7=14 +1=15, so 5 and carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:3+7=10 +1=11, so 1 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:9+6=15 +1=16, so 6 and carryover 1.\n\nThen the million's place: the carried over 1.\n\nSo the total would be 1 (million) 6 (hundred thousands) 1 (ten thousands) 5 (thousands) 0 (hundreds) 1 (tens) 8 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
