n5. **Ten thousands place**: \\(6 + 9 = 15\\) (write down 5, carry over 1)\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \\(9 + 3 + 1 = 13\\) (write down 3, carry over 1)\n7. **Millions place**: The carried over 1 is written down.\n\nCombining all the digits from right to left, we get the result: 1,359,565.\n\nTo verify, we can subtract 390,365 from the result to check if we get 969,200:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n1359565 \\\\\n-390365 \\\\\n\\hline\n969200 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThe subtraction confirms the result is correct. Therefore, the sum of 969,200 and 390,365 is \\(\\boxed{1359565}\\).",
