nes place):.\n\nOnes: 5 + 7 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 8 + 1 = 9, plus the 1 carried over is 10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 2 = 7, plus 1 is 8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 2 + 5 = 7, plus the 1 carried over is 8. Write 8.\n\nSo putting all the digits together: 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
