ds). 9 + 9 = 18. So write 8 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 + 8 = 16, plus the carried 1 is 17. So that's 7 in the hundred thousands and carry over 1 to the millions place, which is a new digit.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:6 (with carryover 1).\n\nHundreds:0 (with carryover 1).\n\nThousands:3.\n\nTen-thousands:8 (with carryover 1).\n\nHundred-thousands:7 (with carryover 1).\n\nMillions place: the carried 1. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
