098 + 712 = 1,810. So total would be 1,447,000 + 1,810 = 1,448,810. Exactly the same as before. So that's a good confirmation.\n\nAlternatively, using another method, maybe adding the numbers from left to right:\n\n781,098 + 667,712.\n\nFirst, add the hundred thousands: 700,000 + 600,000 = 1,300,000.\n\nThen the ten thousands: 80,000 + 60,000 = 140,000. Total so far: 1,440,000.\n\nThousands: 1,000 + 7,000 = 8,000. Total: 1,448,000.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 700 = 700. Total: 1,448,700.\n\nTens: 90 + 10 = 100. Wait, hold on, maybe this approach is getting mixed up. Let me see:\n\nWait, breaking down each number's digits:\n\n781,098:\n\n- 7 (hundred thousands)\n\n- 8 (ten thousands)\n\n- 1 (thousands)\n\n- 0 (hundreds)\n\n- 9 (tens)\n\n- 8 (ones)\n\n667,712:\n\n- 6 (hundred thousands)\n\n- 6 (ten thousands)\n\n- 7 (thousands)\n\n- 7 (hundreds)\n\n- 1 (tens)\n\n- 2 (ones)\n\nAdding each place:\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 6 = 13 \u2192 3 with a carryover of 1.\n\nTen thousands: 8 + 6 = 14 + carryover 1 = 15 \u2192 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 1 + 7 = 8 + 1 = 9, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds: 0 +7 =7.\n\nTens:9 +1=10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1.\n\nOnes:8 +2=10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1.\n\nWait, this approach might not be the best. Wait, actually, when adding left to right, you have to handle the carries differently.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to structure it properly.\n\nAlternatively, let me try adding them digit by digit again but writing it out:\n\n      781098\n\n    +667712\n\n    ---------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 + 2 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens: 9 + 1 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 0 +7 =7 +1=8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nThousands:1 +7=8. Write 8.\n\nTen-thousands:8 +6=14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:7 +6=13 +1=14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 1 carried over. So the total is 1,448,810. \n\nYes, that seems consistent. \n\nAlternatively, let me use another method: calculator style.\n\nBut since I can't use a calculator, maybe subtract