housands, 2 thousands, 9 hundreds, 6 tens, and 3 ones.\n\n925,244 is 9 hundred thousands, 2 ten thousands, 5 thousands, 2 hundreds, 4 tens, and 4 ones.\n\nSo when aligned properly:.\n\n        2 1 2 9 6 3.\n      + 9 2 5 2 4 4.\n      ===============.\n        .\nStarting from the right again:.\n\nOnes: 3 + 4 = 7.\n\nTens: 6 + 4 = 10, write 0 carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 2 = 11, plus 1 carried over is 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 2 + 5 = 7, plus 1 is 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nTen-thousands: 1 + 2 = 3. Write 3.\n\nHundred-thousands: 2 + 9 = 11. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
