ht. Let me confirm the positions again. Let's write the numbers with commas to clarify:.\n\n791,875 is 7 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\n761,596 is 7 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nStarting from the ones:.\n\nOnes: 5 + 6 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 7 + 9 = 16 + 1 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 5 = 13 +1 =14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\nThousands: 1 + 1 = 2 +1 =3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands: 9 +6 =15. Since there's no previous carryover, that's 15. So write 5 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 +7 =14 +1 (carryover) =15. So write 15.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:1, Tens:7, Hundreds:4, Thousands:3, Ten thousands:5 (with a carryover), Hundred thousands:15. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
