he right:.\n\nOnes: 8 + 4 = 12 → 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 1 (carry) + 1 + 5 = 7 → 7, no carryover.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 5 = 9 → 9.\n\nThousands: 8 + 1 = 9 →9.\n\nTen-thousands: 9 +1 =10 →0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 +6 +1 (carryover) =8 →8.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left: 2 (ones), 7 (tens), 9 (hundreds), 9 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
