h no! I made a mistake here. Let me correct that.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nAdding the hundred thousands place: 7 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 13. So, since this is the hundred thousands place, 13 hundred thousands is equal to 1,300,000. Therefore, we write down 3 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since neither number has a millions digit, the carryover becomes the millions digit.\n\nTherefore, putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 4.\n\nHundreds: 7.\n\nThousands: 9.\n\nTen thousands: 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 3 (with a carryover of 1 to millions).\n\nMillions: 1 (from the carryover). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
