. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 8 = 10, plus 1 is 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 8 (from 698,259) + 1 (from 501,873) = 9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 (from 698,259) + 0 (since 501,873 has 0 in the ten thousands place) = 9, plus 1 is 10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 + 5 = 11, plus 1 is 12. So we write 12 here.\n\nSo putting all the digits together: 12 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 2 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
