lions place. Since both original numbers are six digits, their sum could be up to seven digits. So the carried over 1 from the hundred thousands place becomes a 1 in the millions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together: the millions place is 1, the hundred thousands is 1, the ten thousands is 7, thousands is 1, hundreds 8, tens 8, and ones 3. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
