er: 578,001.\n- 5 (hundred thousands).\n- 7 (ten thousands).\n- 8 (thousands).\n- 0 (hundreds).\n- 0 (tens).\n- 1 (units).\n\nAdding them column by column:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 2 + 1 = 3  .\nTens: 6 + 0 = 6  .\nHundreds: 6 + 0 = 6  .\nThousands: 0 + 8 = 8  .\nTen-thousands: 3 + 7 = 10 (write 0, carryover 1)  .\nHundred-thousands: 7 + 5 = 12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\n1,3 (hundred thousands) followed by 0 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
