6 plus 1 is 7\n\nHundred-thousands:7 +9 =16 (write 6, carryover 1)\n\nMillions: 1\n\nSo the result is 1,678,489. All methods confirm this. So I think that's the correct answer. I must have made an error in my first calculation when I thought the thousands digit was 1, but after correcting that, everything checks out. Therefore, the sum is 1,678,489.\n</think>\n\nThe sum of 719,272 and 959,217 is calculated as follows:\n\n```\n  719272\n+ 959217\n---------\n 1678489\n```\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Ones Place:** 2 + 7 = 9  \n2. **Tens Place:** 7 + 1 = 8  \n3. **Hundreds Place:** 2 + 2 = 4  \n4. **Thousands Place:** 9 + 9 = 18 (Write 8, carry over 1)  \n5. **Ten-Thousands Place:** 1 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 7  \n6. **Hundred-Thousands Place:** 7 + 9 = 16 (Write 6, carry over 1)  \n7. **Millions Place:** Carry over 1 becomes the millions digit.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{1678489}",
