2\n\n1s:2+5=7\n\nWait, but this is without considering the carryovers. Wait, actually, when adding columns, you have to carry over to the next higher place. So let me do that properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (1s):\n\n1s:2+5=7. No carryover.\n\n10s:1+1=2. No carryover.\n\n100s:9+5=14. So 4 in 100s place, carryover 1 to 1,000s.\n\n1,000s:4+6=10, plus the carried 1 is 11. So 1 in the 1,000s place, carryover 1 to 10,000s.\n\n10,000s:2+9=11, plus the carried 1 is 12. So 2 in 10,000s, carryover 1 to 100,000s.\n\n100,000s:7+1=8, plus the carried 1 is 9.\n\nSo the total is 9 (100,000s), 2 (10,000s), 1 (1,000s), 4 (100s), 2 (10s), 7 (1s): 921,427.\n\nYes, that's consistent again. So I think that's the correct answer. Let me just check once more with a calculator-like approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\n724,912 + 196,515.\n\nFirst add 724,912 + 100,000 = 824,912.\n\nThen add 96,000: 824,912 + 96,000 = 920,912.\n\nThen add 500: 920,912 + 500 = 921,412.\n\nThen add 10: 921,412 + 10 = 921,422.\n\nThen add 5: 921,422 +5 = 921,427.\n\nYes, that works. So multiple methods give the same result, so I can be confident that 724,912 plus 196,515 is 921,427.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 724912 and 196515 is \\boxed{921427}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 724,912 and 196,515, we start by aligning the numbers vertically and adding each column from right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\begin{array}{cccccc}\n7 & 2 & 4 & 9 & 1 & 2 \\\\\n+ & 1 & 9 & 6 & 5 & 1 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n1. **Ones place**: \\(2 + 5 = 7\\)\n2. **Tens place**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)\n3. **Hundreds place**: \\(9 + 5 = 14\\) (write 4, carry over 1)\n4. **Thousands place**: \\(4 + 6 + 1 = 11\\) (write 1, carry over 1)\n5. **Ten-thousands place**: \\(2 + 9 + 1 = 12\\) (write 2, carry over 1)\n6. **Hundred-thousands place**: \\(7 + 1 + 1 = 9\\)\n\nPutting all the digits together, we get the result 921,427. Verifying through