er is 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 3 + 3 = 6, plus 1 carried over is 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 6 = 13. Write 13.\n\nPutting all together: 13 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
