 (1).\n\nSo when adding, aligning each digit:.\n\nHundreds of thousands: 1 + 2 = 3.\n\nTen thousands: 0 + 9 = 9.\n\nThousands: 4 + 9 = 13.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 0 = 2.\n\nTens: 0 + 6 = 6.\n\nOnes: 3 + 0 = 3.\n\nWait, so the thousands place is 4 +9, which is 13. So that would be 3 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the ten thousands?.\n\nWait, but the ten thousands place was 0 +9, but if we have a carryover from thousands, it would be 9 +1 =10. Then that carryover would go to the hundred thousands place. Hmm, let me do this step by step.\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:.\n\n      1 0 4 2 0 3.\n    + 2 9 9 0 6 0.\n    ----------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 3 + 0 = 3.\n\nTens: 0 + 6 = 6.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 0 = 2.\n\nThousands: 4 + 9 = 13. So write down 3, carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands: 0 + 9 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 + 2 = 3, plus the carried over 1 makes 4. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
