rried over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together: Starting from the right, the digits we got were 3 (ones), 0 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (hundred thousands), and then the 1 in the millions place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
