other method: calculator style.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers digit by digit again.\n\nWait, maybe I can add 556,238 + 496,652 by adding 556,238 + 500,000 first, then subtract the difference. Wait, since 496,652 is 500,000 - 3,348.\n\nSo, 556,238 + 500,000 = 1,056,238.\n\nThen subtract 3,348: 1,056,238 - 3,348.\n\nLet's compute that. 1,056,238 minus 3,000 is 1,053,238. Then minus 348 more: 1,053,238 - 348 = 1,052,890. Same answer again. So that's good. So it seems the answer is 1,052,890. \n\nAlternatively, another check: using approximate rounding. Let's see, 556,238 is approximately 556,000 and 496,652 is approximately 497,000. Adding those gives 556k +497k = 1,053,000. The exact answer is 1,052,890, which is 110 less than the approximation, which makes sense because the first number was rounded down by 238 and the second by 348 (since 496,652 rounded to nearest thousand is 497k, so that's +348). Wait, actually, 496,652 minus 497,000 is -348, so actually, the approximation is overestimating the second number by 348. Therefore the total approximation would overestimate by 348 -238 = 110. So exact answer is 1,053,000 - 110 = 1,052,890. That matches. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another method: adding left to right. Let me try that.\n\nStarting with the hundred thousands:\n\n500,000 + 400,000 = 900,000.\n\nThen ten thousands: 50,000 + 90,000 = 140,000. Total so far 900k +140k = 1,040,000.\n\nThousands: 6,000 +6,000 =12,000. Total 1,052,000.\n\nHundreds: 200 +600=800. Total 1,052,800.\n\nTens:30 +50=80. Total 1,052,880.\n\nOnes:8+2=10. Total 1,052,890.\n\nSame result again. Alright, so I think this must be correct. So the answer is 1,052,890. I'll just make sure I didn't misalign any digits when I first wrote them down, but since multiple methods give the same result, I think it's safe. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do a quick check using digit sums for casting out nines, but that might be overkill. Let me see.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n556,23