ands) + 1 (carry) = 15, so write 5 and carry 1. The carried 1 is the million's place.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 2 (ones). Wait, no:\n\nWait, the places:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:2\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:5\n\nTen thousands:1 (but with a carried over 1 making it 11, so the digit here is 1 and carryover 1)\n\nHundred thousands: 8+6 + the carried over 1?\n\nWait, maybe my confusion is in the placement. Let me think of each digit position:\n\nLet me number the places:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPosition 1 (units): 0 +2 =2.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):1+7=8.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):6+1=7.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6+9=15. So write 5, carryover 1 to position5.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1 (from first number) +9 (from second) =10, plus the carried over 1 is 11. So here, we write 1 and carryover 1 to position6.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):8 +6 =14, plus the carried over 1 is 15. So write 5 here and carryover 1 to position7.\n\nPosition7 (millions place): the carried over 1. So that is the digit in millions place.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from position7 to position1:\n\nPosition7:1,\n\nPosition6:5,\n\nPosition5:1,\n\nPosition4:5,\n\nPosition3:7,\n\nPosition2:8,\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nSo the number is 1,515,782. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do this addition using another method, like expanding the numbers:\n\n816,610 = 800,000 + 16,000 + 600 + 60 +10\n\n699,172 = 600,000 + 99,000 + 100 +70 +2\n\nWait, maybe not the best approach. Alternatively, adding the numbers as is:\n\n816,610\n\n+699,172\n\nLet me add the units: 0+2=2\n\nTens:1+7=8\n\nHundreds:6+1=7\n\nThousands:6+9=15. So 15,000. So 5 in thousands place, carryover 1 to the next (ten thousands).\n\nTen thousands: 1 (from 816,610's ten thousands place is 1, since it's 8-1-6-6-1-0) Wait, wait, actually let me clarify the place values:\n\nWait, 816,610 is brok